    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37895" root="لقث" body-key="l">
    
      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقَثَ</span></b> , [aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقُثَ</span></b> ,] inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقْثٌ</span>; and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لقّث</span></b> , inf. n.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَلْقِيثٌ</span>; <i>He mixed</i> [a thing]. (K.) [The
former verb is as above accord. to the TK: but
it seems to be implied in the K that it is <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِثَ</span>,
aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِثَ</span>, as well in the above sense as in that here
following.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِثَ</span>, aor. 
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقِثَ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">لَقْثٌ</span>, <i>He took</i>
[a thing] <i>quickly, and altogether.</i> (K.) But
this is not of established authority. (TA.)

